The Veil Mother is the neutral elite of the Mistweaver. Its weather lasts
seven rounds, its Fog hides the company and, at the top rank, keeps foes with
extended reach from finding the back row.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Long weather   its weather calls last four rounds longer than a Shaman's
                    (seven in all)
  35 Mother's veil  Fog gives allies +10 Evasion
  40 Deep reserves  +25% maximum mana
  45 Spell edge     +25% spell damage
  50 Heavy mist     Fog gives allies +12 Evasion
  55 Hearth's hide  +4 armor and +20% spell damage
  60 Hidden ranks   while its Fog lasts, foes cannot reach the company's back
                    row with extended reach

It needs the Mistweaver first (<ansi fg="command">help shaman-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] veil-mother confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Shaman talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Deep Reserves (+10% maximum mana),
Spell Edge (+10% spell damage), Focused Will (blows break your chant 25% less
often). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help shaman-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
